title: Table3A
---
// Talk target of the chair at Samantha's table (Interact layer). Her notebook lies on it.
-> Sit down <<if visited("Route1DinnerDoor") and not visited("Route1Dinner")>>
    <<next_scene Route1Dinner>>
-> Open the wine <<if $item_corkscrew>>
    <<set $item_corkscrew to false>>
    <<set $r1_thu2_wine_open to true>>
    <<note_done thu2_cork2>>
    You: There.
    {$samantha_name}: Two glasses. Not to the top.
-> Sit down <<if visited("Route1Thu2Door") and not visited("Route1Thu2Dinner") and ($r1_thu2_wine == "" or $r1_thu2_wine_open)>>
    <<next_scene Route1Thu2Dinner>>
-> Sit down <<if visited("Route1Thu2Door") and not visited("Route1Thu2Dinner") and $r1_thu2_wine != "" and not $r1_thu2_wine_open>>
    {$samantha_name}: Wine first. Corkscrew. Drawer. Sink.
-> Look at her notebook <<if visited("Route1Thu2Door") and not visited("Route1Thu2Dinner")>>
    You: Her notebook. Closed, with a pen clipped to it.
-> Open her notebook <<if visited("Route1Thu2Door") and not visited("Route1Thu2Dinner") and $r1_thu2_notebook == "">>
    <<set $r1_thu2_notebook to "reached">>
    {$samantha_name}: Ah.
    {$samantha_name}: That's mine.
-> Look <<if not (visited("Route1Thu2Door") and not visited("Route1Thu2Dinner"))>>
    <<if visited("Route1Dinner") and not visited("Route1Dishes")>>
        {$samantha_name}: Dinner's over. The sink isn't going to come to you.
    <<else>>
        You: Her table. Her notebook on it, closed.
    <<endif>>
===
